        ("What does event.stopPropagation() do?", "stopPropagation() prevents the event from bubbling up (or capturing down) the DOM tree to ancestor elements.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "e.stopPropagation();", "Does stopPropagation prevent handlers on the same element from running?"),
        ("What does event.stopImmediatePropagation() do?", "stopImmediatePropagation() prevents the event from propagating to ancestor elements AND prevents any other listeners on the current element from executing.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "e.stopImmediatePropagation();", "How does this differ from stopPropagation?"),
        ("What are the three phases of DOM event propagation?", "1. Capturing phase (event travels down from window to target). 2. Target phase (event reaches the target element). 3. Bubbling phase (event bubbles up from target to window).", "Intermediate", "Concept", "", "In which phase do listeners run by default?"),
