        ("What is event capturing (trickling)?", "Event capturing is the phase where the event travels down from the root window through ancestors toward the target element before bubbling begins.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "el.addEventListener('click', handler, { capture: true });", "How do you enable capturing in addEventListener?"),
        ("How do you enable the capturing phase in addEventListener?", "Pass true as the third argument or pass { capture: true } in the options object.", "Intermediate", "Practical", "el.addEventListener('click', handler, { capture: true });", "Which runs first: capturing or bubbling listener?"),
        ("What is event delegation?", "Event delegation is a pattern of attaching a single event listener to a parent element to handle events for all current and future child elements using event bubbling.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "list.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n  if (e.target.matches('li')) console.log(e.target.textContent);\n});", "Why is event delegation beneficial for dynamic lists?"),
        ("Why is event delegation good for performance and memory?", "Instead of creating hundreds of separate event listeners for every child element, a single parent listener consumes much less memory and automatically handles dynamically added children.", "Intermediate", "Scenario", "", "Can non-bubbling events use delegation?"),
