        ("What does the { passive: true } option in addEventListener do?", "It indicates that the handler will never call preventDefault(), allowing the browser to scroll smoothly on mobile touch/wheel events without waiting for JS execution.", "Intermediate", "Practical", "window.addEventListener('touchstart', onTouch, { passive: true });", "What happens if preventDefault is called in a passive listener?"),
