        ("What does .replaceWith() do in jQuery?", ".replaceWith(newContent) replaces each matched element with the provided new content or element.", "Easy", "Practical", "$('#old-btn').replaceWith('<button id=\"new-btn\">Updated</button>');", "What does .replaceAll() do?"),
        ("What does .attr() do in jQuery?", ".attr(name) gets the value of an attribute on the first matched element, or sets attribute values on all matched elements.", "Easy", "Practical", "const src = $('img').attr('src');\n$('img').attr('alt', 'Thumbnail');", "How do you set multiple attributes at once with .attr()?"),
        ("How do you set multiple attributes simultaneously using .attr()?", "Pass a plain JavaScript object: $('img').attr({ src: 'pic.jpg', alt: 'Profile', title: 'User' }).", "Easy", "Practical", "$('img').attr({\n  src: 'avatar.png',\n  alt: 'Avatar'\n});", "What does .removeAttr() do?"),
        ("What does .removeAttr() do in jQuery?", ".removeAttr(attributeName) removes the specified attribute from each matched element.", "Easy", "Practical", "$('button').removeAttr('disabled');", "How does .prop() differ from .attr()?"),
        ("What is the critical difference between .attr() and .prop() in jQuery?", ".attr() retrieves the HTML attribute value written in the HTML markup. .prop() retrieves the live JavaScript DOM property value (e.g. checked, disabled, selected).", "Intermediate", "Comparison", "$('#cb').prop('checked'); // true or false\n$('#cb').attr('checked'); // 'checked' or undefined", "Which should you use for checkbox checked status?"),
        ("Why should you use .prop('checked') instead of .attr('checked')?", "Because checked is a dynamic boolean property. After user interaction, .attr('checked') does not reflect user toggling, but .prop('checked') always reflects live state.", "Intermediate", "Scenario", "", "What does .removeProp() do?"),
        ("What does .data() do in jQuery?", ".data(key, value) stores or reads arbitrary data associated with matched elements in jQuery's internal memory store and reads HTML5 data-* attributes.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "$('#user').data('role', 'admin');\nconsole.log($('#user').data('role'));", "Does .data() update the HTML attribute in DOM inspection?"),
