        ("Does jQuery automatically add 'px' when setting numeric CSS properties?", "Yes, for dimension properties (width, height, top, margin), jQuery automatically converts raw numbers (e.g. width: 300) to '300px'.", "Easy", "Concept", "$('#box').css('width', 300); // Sets 300px", "Which properties do NOT get px appended?"),
        ("What is the difference between .width() and .css('width') in jQuery?", ".width() returns a unitless number (e.g. 300). .css('width') returns a string with units (e.g. '300px').", "Intermediate", "Comparison", "const num = $('#box').width(); // 300 (number)\nconst str = $('#box').css('width'); // '300px' (string)", "Which is better for mathematical calculations?"),
        ("What does .innerWidth() measure in jQuery?", ".innerWidth() measures the width including padding, but excluding borders and margins.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "innerWidth = width + padding", "What does innerHeight measure?"),
