        ("What does .slideUp() do in jQuery?", ".slideUp() hides an element with a sliding motion by animating its height to 0, then sets display: none.", "Easy", "Practical", "$('#accordion-content').slideUp(300);", "What does .slideToggle() do?"),
        ("What does .slideToggle() do in jQuery?", ".slideToggle() slides an element up or down depending on its current visibility state (ideal for accordions and dropdowns).", "Easy", "Practical", "$('#faq-answer').slideToggle(250);", "Why is slideToggle popular for accordions?"),
        ("What does the .animate() method in jQuery do?", ".animate(properties, duration, easing, callback) performs custom animations of numeric CSS properties on matched elements.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "$('#box').animate({\n  left: '+=50px',\n  opacity: 0.8\n}, 500);", "Can .animate() animate color properties natively?"),
        ("Why can't jQuery .animate() animate color properties (like backgroundColor) by default?", "Core jQuery can only animate numeric properties. Color animation requires the jQuery Color plugin or CSS transitions.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "", "What is preferred for color transitions today?"),
