        ("What causes animation queue buildup (animation flicker) in jQuery?", "Triggering mouse hover events repeatedly queues up animations in jQuery's internal animation queue, causing the element to keep animating after the user stops hovering.", "Intermediate", "Scenario", "", "How does .stop(true, true) solve animation queue buildup?"),
        ("What do the two boolean arguments in .stop(clearQueue, jumpToEnd) do?", "clearQueue (first boolean) clears all queued animations. jumpToEnd (second boolean) immediately completes the current animation.", "Intermediate", "Practical", "$('#box').stop(true, false).slideDown();", "Which configuration prevents hover buildup?"),
        ("What does .finish() do in jQuery?", ".finish() stops the currently-running animation, clears all queued animations, and immediately completes all animations in the queue.", "Intermediate", "Practical", "$('#box').finish();", "How does .finish differ from .stop(true, true)?"),
        ("What does .delay() do in jQuery?", ".delay(duration) sets a timer to delay execution of subsequent items in the jQuery animation queue.", "Easy", "Practical", "$('#alert').fadeIn(300).delay(2000).fadeOut(300);", "Does .delay work with non-animation functions?"),
