        ("How do you load only a specific portion of a page using .load()?", "Append a page selector after the URL: $('#container').load('/page.html #target-div').", "Intermediate", "Practical", "$('#container').load('/page.html #sidebar');", "Why is this useful for tabs?"),
        ("What are the promise callback methods on jQuery $.ajax() objects?", ".done(successCallback), .fail(errorCallback), and .always(completeCallback).", "Intermediate", "Concept", "$.get('/api/data')\n  .done(data => console.log(data))\n  .fail(err => console.error(err))\n  .always(() => console.log('Finished'));", "What did .done() replace in older jQuery?"),
        ("Why were success and error options in $.ajax deprecated in favor of .done() and .fail()?", ".done() and .fail() follow standard Promise chaining conventions, allowing multiple callbacks and better asynchronous composition.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "", "Are $.ajax returned objects true Promises in jQuery 3?"),
        ("What does $(form).serialize() do in jQuery?", ".serialize() encodes form elements as a URL-encoded query string (e.g. 'name=John&age=25') ready for GET or POST submission.", "Easy", "Practical", "const queryString = $('#myForm').serialize();\n$.post('/api/submit', queryString);", "What elements are excluded by .serialize()?"),
        ("What elements does .serialize() exclude from the query string?", "Disabled inputs, buttons, file inputs, and unchecked checkboxes or radio buttons.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "", "What does .serializeArray() do?"),
